        record claimed five script families, which is a list rather than a consistency boundary"
}

// The regex half, retired by TS.260821.07.
//
// Both learned what this plugin contains by matching a pattern against the working tree.
// The fragile thing about that was never the pattern: it was that the prose WAS the state,
// so the pattern was the only reader, and the only way to find out it had stopped matching
// was for somebody to notice the output looked wrong.
//
// Neither is a doctrine-surface by kind — a generator is not instruction — but both are
// recorded here because retiring them is what TS.260821.07 DID, and a removal nobody wrote
// down is indistinguishable from a removal nobody made.
doctrine-surface "surface.retired.gen-coverage-matrix" {
    path "scripts/gen-coverage-matrix.sh"
    kind "probe"
    serves "TS.260821.07"
    state "retired"
    retired-at "2026-08-22"
    stands-at "v0.7.1"
    because "it derived the coverage matrix by grepping every probe's --include list. Language \
        coverage is now a field on the invariant, declared by whoever writes the probe, and a \
        structural probe SAYS so instead of being listed against nine languages it does not scan"
}

doctrine-surface "surface.retired.gen-doctrine-index" {
    path "scripts/gen-doctrine-index.sh"
    kind "probe"
    serves "TS.260821.07"
    state "retired"
    retired-at "2026-08-22"
    stands-at "v0.7.1"
    because "it scraped the instruction files frontmatter into a table inside generated \
        markers, and CI failed on a hand-edit within them. It kept one table honest about a set \
        of files nothing else could describe at all"
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The two front doors, retired by TS.260823.08.
//
// They split greenfield from brownfield, and both installed the spine TS.260821.04 deleted:
// a wave directory, a sprint placeholder, fifty-one overlay templates and a generated
// verify.sh calling two probes this plugin does not ship. Neither named the delivery graph
// once. `adopt-the-method` was correct and third in the index, so nobody reached it.
//
// The split was never the useful axis. What a repository needs on arrival is the same
// whether or not it already has code: a binding, a gate that can run, and the engineering
// doctrine that was never spine-bound. `praxis adopt` writes those three and nothing else.
//
// The files are removed, not shimmed. v0.7.1 is tagged; every one is recoverable by name
// with `git checkout v0.7.1 -- <path>`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

doctrine-surface "surface.retired.bootstrap-project" {
    path "skills/bootstrap-project/SKILL.md"
    kind "skill"
    serves "TS.260823.08"
    state "retired"
    retired-at "2026-08-23"
    stands-at "v0.7.1"
    because "it scaffolded a bootstrap wave directory, a sprint placeholder and a wave \
        dashboard, in a method that has none of the three. Twenty of its lines instructed an \
        agent in a kind the record had retired two versions earlier"
}

doctrine-surface "surface.retired.provision-project-overlay" {
    path "skills/provision-project-overlay/SKILL.md"
    kind "skill"
    serves "TS.260823.08"
    state "retired"
    retired-at "2026-08-23"
    stands-at "v0.7.1"
    because "it emitted fifty-one template files — sixteen skill templates, eleven prompts, the \
        persona overlays and a YAML config of its own — into an adopter's repository. The \
        engineering half survived on its own merits and is rewritten as one pointer file; the \
        spine half had nothing left to describe"
}

doctrine-surface "surface.retired.overlay-templates" {
    path "skills/provision-project-overlay/templates/"
    kind "skill"
    serves "TS.260823.08"
    state "retired"
    retired-at "2026-08-23"
    stands-at "v0.7.1"
    because "the fifty-one files TS.260823.05 revealed and declared as debt on the \
        `ships-doctrine` shape. They are retired as one act because they were written as one \
        act: a tree copied whole into an adopter's repository, teaching waves, sprints, \
        initiatives and TS-NNN ids in every file that had a verb in it"
    note "one declaration for a directory, not fifty-one for its files. The engine anchors by \
        PATH and no file at this path ships, so nothing here is a promise the record cannot \
        keep — and fifty-one retirement stanzas saying the same sentence would bury the one \
        fact a reader needs, which is that the tree is gone"
}

doctrine-surface "surface.retired.overlay-manifest" {
    path "skills/provision-project-overlay/manifest.yaml"
    kind "skill"
    serves "TS.260823.08"
    state "retired"
    retired-at "2026-08-23"
    stands-at "v0.7.1"
    because "the managed-file list the overlay emitted from. What adoption writes is now four \
        files named in the engine, derived from the record of what ships — a manifest is a \
        second copy of that list, and the two would drift the way every other pair has"
}
